      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "src/tools/newProject.ts gains a process-local rolling-window rate-limit of 5 calls per 60s for runNewProjectStart.",
        "When exceeded, runNewProjectStart returns a new error code `rate_limited` with a hint stating the window length and that it resets on a per-process basis.",
        "Inside the 5-call window, calls succeed normally.",
        "After the 60s window slides past the oldest call, capacity is restored.",
        "Test-only helper `_resetNewProjectStateForTests` clears the rate-limit window in addition to existing state.",
        "tests/unit (existing or new file) has at least 3 cases: under-limit calls succeed (mocked HTTP), 6th call within window returns rate_limited, after-window-slide call succeeds again. Use a fake clock or short window override (e.g. via env VERSE8_RATE_WINDOW_MS for testing).",
